<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-10-03T19:18:44Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Morocco's first female head of government: Symbol or real reform?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:696bee2c524dcb5f8433da2441c55109e255a63e7f2f43ec1c863fd4a94b5790</id><updated>2026-10-03T19:18:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/morocco-s-first-female-head-of-government-symbol-or-real-reform/a-79521808--5c6131d5d637.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/morocco-s-first-female-head-of-government-symbol-or-real-reform/a-79521808?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fatima Zahra Mansouri has been chosen as Morocco's first female prime minister. Is her appointment a kind of symbolism, to show Morocco in a positive light? Or could Mansouri bring genuine changes for Moroccan women?</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Aliko Dangote: What is the secret to his success across Africa?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:336fdec802362a64dc9e4c0bc6aaf139303d6afbb0bd493f2b50d8ae6242ab63</id><updated>2026-10-03T19:18:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/aliko-dangote-what-is-the-secret-to-his-success-across-africa/a-79500035--de5ccc5df6f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/aliko-dangote-what-is-the-secret-to-his-success-across-africa/a-79500035?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nigerian entrepreneur Aliko Dangote bets billions on Africa's future. The expansion of his industrial empire on the continent is unprecedented. Has Dangote cracked the code to business success in Africa, and if so — how?</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Growing fear of war in the Horn of Africa after Eritrea cuts ties with Ethiopia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa20e4c9374cacfbef413eeb88c42e205df55bea94ec9abbe4ef8d67912ede1e</id><updated>2026-10-03T19:18:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/growing-fear-of-war-in-the-horn-of-africa-after-eritrea-cuts-ties-with-ethiopia/a-79513311--226a98e4fbfb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/growing-fear-of-war-in-the-horn-of-africa-after-eritrea-cuts-ties-with-ethiopia/a-79513311?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Tigray conflict is no longer just a domestic issue. As Ethiopia, Eritrea and Egypt trade accusations, the African Union (AU) urges restraint. Is the Horn of Africa hurtling toward a wider regional crisis?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: Who could bring the warring sides to the negotiation table?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6220bb3157d8f0ecf0f51edec0cdae8eb02c8d37e946459b4b95496fcd80ccd</id><updated>2026-10-03T19:18:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-who-could-bring-the-warring-sides-to-the-negotiation-table/a-79475529--2936c02781db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-who-could-bring-the-warring-sides-to-the-negotiation-table/a-79475529?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia might be facing its most complex armed conflict in contemporary times. The fragile 2022 peace deal has collapsed. International mediators have failed. How will the country return to normal?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Five EU states plan first deportation center in Africa for 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13c0e28f170b521025d902385c1de7834ff75decd575ef6505bf0df146298e65</id><updated>2026-10-03T19:18:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162--dbd1d60c3bb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Greece, Germany, Austria, Denmark and the Netherlands are moving forward with plans to establish deportation centers for rejected asylum seekers outside the EU.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal's Youth Olympics makes Olympics in Africa 'logical'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:169984085d644b89ea72d29c527dc0b42f092b0b5ec517d9d68894c908f078f5</id><updated>2026-10-03T19:18:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/senegal-s-youth-olympics-makes-olympics-in-africa-logical/a-79468975--7dbe2801c775.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/senegal-s-youth-olympics-makes-olympics-in-africa-logical/a-79468975?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Youth Olympics are to be hosted in Africa for the first time ever. The edition in Senegal is also a chance to prove the continent can host a full Olympics in the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
